# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-owned-com-close-reads-partial-result -- close-owned-com-bridge reads close-owned.result before it is written
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-alfe-owned-com-close-reads-partial-result
#+DATE: 2026-11-04

* Symptom

test:alfe:ccl failed on MR !509 (pipeline 3027406641, job 17737727775), with
2428/2429 checks passing:

: OWNED-COM-CLOSE-REQUIRES-PROCESS-EXIT-RESULT in AUTOLISP-FRONT-END-SUITE []:
:      Unexpected Error: #<ALFE.ERROR:BACKEND-PROTOCOL-ERROR>
: alfe CAD backend error (phase SHUTDOWN): The owned CAD did not close normally. [OWNED-CAD-CLOSE-FAILED].

The same test passed on master's pipeline for c3944cbe. The MR does not touch
backend-cad-common.lisp: the failure is a race.

* Cause

=close-owned-com-bridge= (autolisp-front-end/source/backend-cad-common.lisp)
loops on =(probe-file result)= and reads the file as soon as it EXISTS. The
writer (the test's worker thread; on Windows, the VBS bridge) creates the file
and then writes "0". A read between the two finds "" and treats it as a
failed close (=:owned-cad-close-failed=) instead of "not yet". On a loaded CI
runner the window is wide enough to hit.

The bridge has the same hazard in production: a slow write of the result
looks like a CAD that did not close.

* Fix

- Treat an empty (whitespace-only) result as "not written yet": keep polling
  until the timeout.
- And/or have the writers write a temporary file and rename it (atomic on
  POSIX; on Windows the reader keeps the empty-means-wait rule, since rename
  is not atomic there -- AGENTS.md, native lanes).
- Regression test: a worker that creates the file, sleeps, then writes "0";
  the close must succeed.
